[123.586308, "o", "f testing distorted the September fieldwork reconciliation. The team reconstructed mailbox ordering and found unsigned amendment drift affecting at least 6 transaction threads.\r\n   847\t\r\n   848\tVendor management S. Patel described revenue cutoff testing onboarding delays that pushed compliance responses past ledger dates on several rejected rows during September fieldwork.\r\n   849\t\r\n   850\tPeer review #598 of external audit sampling found 20 mislinked emails on revenue cutoff testing. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.\r\n   851\t\r\n   852\tFollow-up #458 confirmed that external audit routed revenue cutoff testing statements through a shared inbox with 3 delegates. Investigators flagged hold flag suppression as the likely root cause of inconsistent status columns.\r\n   853\t\r\n   854\tQuality review #450 sampled 22 revenue cutoff testing tickets and found policy waiver omission whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.\r\n "]
[123.586455, "o", "  855\t\r\n   856\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n   857\t\r\n   858\tAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n   859\tledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n   860\tsets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n   861\t`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n   862\tkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n   863\tplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n   864\t\r\n   865\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output — supporting chronology"]
[123.587299, "o", "\r\n   866\t\r\n   867\tInternal audit follow-up #770 tracked how vendor onboarding backlog exceptions were closed without matching policy waiver paperwork, a separate issue from extractor merge ordering.\r\n   868\t\r\n   869\tStakeholder workshop #200 on vendor onboarding backlog produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n   870\t\r\n   871\tPrivacy review #629 redacted personal data from vendor onboarding backlog threads but retained transaction identifiers needed for reconciliation testing.\r\n   872\t\r\n   873\tLead reviewer J. Huang opened working paper WP-9697 after procurement reported that vendor onboarding backlog distorted the Q1 close reconciliation. The team reconstructed mailbox ordering and found ledger slice confusion affecting at least 4 transaction threads.\r\n   874\t\r\n   875\tMemo WP-8092 summarizes a panel on vendor onboarding backlog chaired by R. Okonkwo. Participants debated whether informal spread"]
