[284.021618, "o", "  1455\t## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n  1456\t\r\n  1457\tMid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n  1458\tamendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n  1459\tonly, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n  1460\tledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n  1461\tin effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n  1462\tbefore any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n  1463\tmail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n  1464\t\r\n  1465\t## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment — supporting chronology\r\n  1466\t\r\n  1467\tTax counsel flagged lease modification restatement restatement risk during August memo close, unrelated to extractor precedence but relevant to why the archive retains full correspondence.\r\n  1468\t\r\n  1469\tPlatform engineer A. Ndiaye noted th"]
[284.021657, "o", "at lease modification restatement webhook retries duplicated compliance messages in the investigative export, requiring deduplication by subject and sent timestamp during human review.\r\n  1470\t\r\n  1471\tIn August memo, technical accounting migrated lease modification restatement workflows to a new ticketing tool. Migration cutover introduced hold flag suppression, which did not reproduce once ledger sourcing rules from Brief 01 were applied manually.\r\n  1472\t\r\n  1473\tGrant compliance WP-5480 tied lease modification restatement attestation gaps to hold flag suppression visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.\r\n  1474\t\r\n  1475\tRisk assessment WP-8316 links lease modification restatement to control gaps in mail ingestion for technical accounting. The assessment explicitly warns against treating alternate ledger headings or appendix commentary as transaction sources.\r\n  1476\t\r\n  1477\tSOX testing team WP-6062 linked ledger slice confusion on lease modification restatement"]
[284.021669, "o", " to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.\r\n  1478\t\r\n  1479\tInternal audit follow-up #581 tracked how lease modification restatement exceptions were closed without matching policy waiver paperwork, a separate issue from extractor merge ordering.\r\n  1480\t\r\n  1481\tDuring August memo, L. Bergstrom compared two cold extractor runs and documented owner field churn on lease modification restatement. Operations initially attributed the drift to cache state; QA disproved that hypothesis the following morning.\r\n  1482\t\r\n  1483\tData governance WP-1783 catalogs legacy technical accounting folders still containing lease modification restatement spreadsheets. Those folders are evidentiary only; extractor output must come from canonical structured sections.\r\n  1484\t\r\n  1485\tPeer review #493 of technical accounting sampling found 14 mislinked emails on lease modification restatement. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sende"]
[284.02168, "o", "r restrictions.\r\n  1486\t\r\n  1487\tExternal advisors reviewing lease modification restatement during August memo asked for a machine-readable trace explaining why rejected rows received hold flags. The archive preserves narrative chronology even though only structured tail sections are authoritative.\r\n  1488\t\r\n  1489\tAudit technologist T. Singh replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how lease modification restatement threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing owner field churn on four high-balance rows.\r\n  1490\t\r\n  1491\tWorking paper WP-4998 documents a three-way match failure on lease modification restatement where accrual true-ups near $14,386 never received matching compliance responses during August memo.\r\n  1492\t\r\n  1493\tStakeholder workshop #608 on lease modification restatement produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n  1494\t\r\n  1495\tCommittee packet #417 chr"]
[284.021691, "o", "onicles how lease modification restatement escalated after J. Huang observed unsigned amendment drift between two correction batches. Cross-checks against amendment minutes were required before accepting any owner change.\r\n"]
