[345.624876, "o", "   214\t## Investigation Brief 02 — Status Precedence\r\n"]
[345.625071, "o", "   215\t\r\n   216\tInterview notes with the compliance desk confirmed status fights between mail,\r\n   217\tamendments, and corrections. Ledger rows provide the base status (lowercase on\r\n   218\toutput). Status precedence from lowest to highest is: pending, approved,\r\n   219\trejected, reversed. Email excerpts may change status only when the From line\r\n   220\tcontains `compliance@` anywhere in the address; ignore all other senders.\r\n   221\t\r\n"]
[345.632539, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[346.544024, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '384,392p'\n"]
[346.545068, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '384,392p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[346.556026, "o", "   384\t## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n   385\t\r\n"]
[346.556797, "o", "   386\tThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n   387\tmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n   388\t`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n   389\tequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n   390\tapply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n   391\tafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n   392\t\r\n"]
[346.558784, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[347.589924, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '555,563p'\n"]
[347.615386, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '555,563p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[347.618845, "o", "   555\t## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n"]
[347.618901, "o", "   556\t\r\n"]
[347.618922, "o", "   557\tThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n"]
[347.61894, "o", "   558\ttarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n"]
[347.618957, "o", "   559\tgreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n"]
[347.618974, "o", "   560\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n"]
[347.618992, "o", "   561\tapplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n"]
[347.619009, "o", "   562\tboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n"]
[347.619025, "o", "   563\t\r\n"]
[347.639243, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[347.639325, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[348.417952, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '672,679p'\n"]
[348.419229, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '672,679p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[348.42885, "o", "   672\t## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n   673\t\r\n   674\tCommittee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n   675\tdefault. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace\r\n   676\towner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n   677\t`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n   678\tledger date for the transaction.\r\n   679\t\r\n"]
[348.430377, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[349.486901, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '856,864p'\n"]
[349.488187, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '856,864p'\r\n"]
[349.488218, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[349.497106, "o", "   856\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n   857\t\r\n   858\tAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n   859\tledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n   860\tsets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n   861\t`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n   862\tkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with two decimal\r\n   863\tplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n   864\t\r\n"]
[349.501947, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[350.414547, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '973,982p'\n"]
[350.418752, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '973,982p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[350.426745, "o", "   973\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n   974\t\r\n   975\tException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n   976\t`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n   977\twhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n   978\tthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n   979\tcomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n   980\t(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n   981\tlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n   982\t\r\n"]
[350.427656, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[350.428278, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[351.564633, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '1145,1152p'\n"]
[351.565018, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '1145,1152p'"]
[351.567821, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[351.588642, "o", "  1145\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II)\r\n  1146\t\r\n  1147\tContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n  1148\t`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n  1149\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n  1150\tfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n  1151\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n  1152\t\r\n"]
[351.59455, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[351.594785, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[352.458084, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '1455,1464p'\n"]
[352.460123, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '1455,1464p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[352.470886, "o", "  1455\t## Investigation Brief 09 — Mid-Year Amendment\r\n  1456\t\r\n  1457\tMid-year QA found compliance holds disappearing after date corrections. This\r\n  1458\tamendment supersedes any earlier wording about hold timing. For `compliance_hold`\r\n  1459\tonly, compare each qualifying email's `sent:` date against the transaction's\r\n  1460\tledger date immediately before correction notices are applied — that is, the date\r\n  1461\tin effect after ledger load, meeting amendments, and compliance mail merges, but\r\n  1462\tbefore any correction notice changes `date` or `status`. Brief 03 still governs\r\n  1463\tmail-driven status changes; this amendment governs only the hold flag.\r\n  1464\t\r\n"]
[352.471235, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[352.473291, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[362.029028, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '11,25p'\n"]
[362.029154, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '11,25p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[362.044378, "o", "    11\t## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing\r\n"]
[362.0447, "o", "    12\t\r\n"]
[362.045108, "o", "    13\tFinance QA traced rerun drift to parsers that latched onto the wrong ledger\r\n    14\tslice. For extractor output, treat only the markdown section whose heading\r\n    15\tline is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also\r\n    16\tcontains a working-copy ledger and prose that mentions ledger headings; those\r\n    17\tare investigative context only.\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tIgnore any ledger block that includes a line `provisional: true` (case\r\n    20\tinsensitive). When the same transaction id appears in multiple non-provisional\r\n    21\tledger blocks, the last such block in file order is the base row for that id.\r\n"]
[362.045596, "o", "    22\t\r\n    23\tLocate section boundaries with regular expressions anchored to whole heading\r\n    24\tlines at line start. Do not locate sections with indexOf or substring search.\r\n    25\t\r\n"]
[362.047061, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[362.047464, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[362.958102, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '384,392p'\n"]
[362.958369, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '384,392p'"]
[362.958417, "o", "\r\n"]
[362.958656, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[362.977067, "o", "   384\t## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n   385\t\r\n   386\tThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n   387\tmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n   388\t`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n   389\tequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n   390\tapply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n   391\tafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n   392\t\r\n"]
[362.983996, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[362.984185, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[363.991324, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '555,563p'\n"]
[363.991563, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '555,563p'"]
[363.991969, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[364.000611, "o", "   555\t## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n   556\t\r\n   557\tThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n   558\ttarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n   559\tgreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n   560\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n   561\tapplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n   562\tboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n   563\t\r\n"]
[364.002134, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[364.002412, "o", "root@edd51c718576:/app# "]
[365.097547, "i", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '672,679p'\n"]
[365.098443, "o", "nl -ba /app/data/audit_archive.md | sed -n '672,679p'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[365.133095, "o", "   672\t## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n   673\t\r\n"]
[365.134245, "o", "   674\tCommittee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n   675\tdefault. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>` replace\r\n   676\towner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n   677\t`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n   678\tledger date for the transaction.\r\n   679\t\r\n"]
